    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="0873" n="759" xml:id="pg759"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">195/609: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-08-23T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1924—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 23—8:53
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>379. My 367, August 13, 4 p.m.<anchor n="41" xml:id="d690-f1"/> Foreign Office
                    has just informed me officially that pending recognition by the French
                    Government of the American Bureau of Shipping, American vessels calling at
                    French ports will in no way be interfered with.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
